  "decisions": {
    "iampennyli/ima-skills": {
      "source_tree_sha256": "b8d1e1dd2efce1ee02c3f34dcf16456c3e5625982d03ba49be6c64e1ff037ddf",
      "reviewer_kind": "assistant_source_review",
      "reviewer_id": "calibration-source-screening-agent",
      "decision": "include",
      "reason": "Source-only review confirms two distinct material workflow features and available own-source content with exact physical quotations. Target outputs, registry scores, scan labels, gold judgments, and DOE conclusions were not used.",
      "features": [
        {
          "feature": "cross_file_dataflow",
          "reason": "Cross-module tasks pass knowledge-base search/read content into note creation, or pass a searched note identifier into knowledge-base insertion, requiring both retained module guides.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "path": "SKILL.md",
              "start_line": 66,
              "end_line": 74,
              "quote": "某些意图跨越 notes 和 knowledge-base 两个模块。**不要只读取一个子模块就开始执行**，必须先读取两个模块的 SKILL.md 再按顺序操作。\n\n| 用户说的                             | 实际流程                                      | 读取顺序                                               |\n| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| \"把知识库里的XX内容记到笔记\"         | KB 搜索/读取 → Notes 创建/追加                | 先读 `knowledge-base/SKILL.md` → 再读 `notes/SKILL.md` |\n| \"查看原文\"（知识库中的笔记类型媒体） | KB `get_media_info` → Notes `get_doc_content` | 先读 `knowledge-base/SKILL.md` → 再读 `notes/SKILL.md` |\n| \"把这篇笔记添加到知识库\"             | Notes 搜索获取 note_id → KB `add_knowledge`   | 先读 `notes/SKILL.md` → 再读 `knowledge-base/SKILL.md` |\n\n**规则**：如果用户意图同时涉及「笔记」和「知识库」，或者 API 响应揭示需要另一个模块（如 `media_type=11` 表示笔记类型），必须读取两个子模块再继续。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "feature": "versions_or_transformations",
          "reason": "Before note writes, string content is explicitly checked or converted to UTF-8 while binary file uploads follow a separate unchanged-content contract.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "path": "SKILL.md",
              "start_line": 191,
              "end_line": 205,
              "quote": "> **此规则为强制性要求，不可跳过。** 非法编码会导致内容在 IMA 中显示为乱码，且无法修复，必须重新写入。\n>\n> **适用范围：notes 模块**（`import_doc`、`append_doc` 等文本写入 API）。\n>\n> **不适用于 knowledge-base 模块的文件上传**：上传文件时必须保持文件原始内容，不得转码。文件以二进制方式上传，服务端自行处理。\n\n**每次调用 notes 写入类 API（`import_doc`/`append_doc`）之前，必须对 `content`、`title` 等所有字符串字段执行 UTF-8 编码校验/转换。** 无论内容来源如何——用户直接输入、从文件读取、WebFetch 抓取、剪贴板粘贴、外部 API 返回——都不能假设已经是合法 UTF-8，必须显式确认。\n\n#### 强制检查清单（notes 模块写入前）\n\n在构造 notes 写入请求的 body **之前**，完成以下步骤：\n\n1. **来自文件的内容**：先检测文件编码，转为 UTF-8 后再读入变量（注意：这是指读取文件内容作为笔记正文写入，不是上传文件到知识库）\n2. **来自 WebFetch / HTTP 请求的内容**：响应可能为 GBK/Latin-1 等，必须转码\n3. **来自用户输入或变量拼接的内容**：清洗非法 UTF-8 字节（`\\xff\\xfe` 等）"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_closure": {
        "status": "complete_for_static_audit",
        "reason": "The notes and knowledge-base module guides, both API references, ima_api.cjs, and the COS/preflight scripts are retained. The preflight basename and implementation are unambiguous under knowledge-base/scripts; the API-reference-relative nomination is not an additional missing body. IMA, COS, credentials, runtime note/file content, and update contexts are external/runtime interfaces. No automatic local path alias is asserted.",
        "local_reference_decisions": [
          {
            "target": "knowledge-base/references/scripts/preflight-check.cjs",
            "classification": "illustrative_or_optional",
            "reason": "The referenced preflight-check.cjs implementation is retained under the knowledge-base module scripts directory; the reference is written within that module guide. The nomination resolves it relative to references/, but no second missing implementation is implied.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "path": "knowledge-base/references/api.md",
                "start_line": 497,
                "end_line": 497,
                "quote": "使用 `scripts/preflight-check.cjs` 脚本自动完成类型检测和大小校验。脚本按以下优先级解析："
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "mahmoudadelbghany/ffmpeg-video-editor": {
      "source_tree_sha256": "b460f91fb430caff0a5d0a03fa5a7c05f255334693088963a52461bd187eb6f0",
      "reviewer_kind": "assistant_source_review",
      "reviewer_id": "calibration-source-screening-agent",
      "decision": "include",
      "reason": "Source-only review confirms two distinct material workflow features and available own-source content with exact physical quotations. Target outputs, registry scores, scan labels, gold judgments, and DOE conclusions were not used.",
      "features": [
        {
          "feature": "versions_or_transformations",
          "reason": "The assistant derives an FFmpeg command from the requested operation and extracted input/output/timestamp/format parameters. The skill generates commands; execution of the resulting media transformation is not assumed.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "path": "SKILL.md",
              "start_line": 8,
              "end_line": 16,
              "quote": "You are a video editing assistant that translates natural language requests into FFmpeg commands. When the user asks to edit a video, generate the correct FFmpeg command.\n\n## How to Generate Commands\n\n1. **Identify the operation** from the user's request\n2. **Extract parameters** (input file, output file, timestamps, formats, etc.)\n3. **Generate the FFmpeg command** using the patterns below\n4. **If output filename not specified**, create one based on the operation (e.g., `video_trimmed.mp4`)\n5. **Always include** `-y` (overwrite) and `-hide_banner` for cleaner output"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "feature": "conditions_or_retries",
          "reason": "If an output filename is absent, command generation supplies an operation-specific output name instead of treating an unspecified path as available.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "path": "SKILL.md",
              "start_line": 12,
              "end_line": 16,
              "quote": "1. **Identify the operation** from the user's request\n2. **Extract parameters** (input file, output file, timestamps, formats, etc.)\n3. **Generate the FFmpeg command** using the patterns below\n4. **If output filename not specified**, create one based on the operation (e.g., `video_trimmed.mp4`)\n5. **Always include** `-y` (overwrite) and `-hide_banner` for cleaner output"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_closure": {
        "status": "complete_for_static_audit",
        "reason": "The command-generation rules and FFmpeg command patterns are all embedded in SKILL.md. FFmpeg and input/output media paths are external/runtime interfaces. No own script is required, and the presence of command examples does not mean this skill executes them automatically.",
        "local_reference_decisions": []
      }
    },
    "goktugcy/tavily-web-search-for-openclaw": {
      "source_tree_sha256": "3b45c666ec911163a037369869197b23a79f08facb576e2776b8ec727675803c",
      "reviewer_kind": "assistant_source_review",
      "reviewer_id": "calibration-source-screening-agent",
      "decision": "include",
      "reason": "Source-only review confirms two distinct material workflow features and available own-source content with exact physical quotations. Target outputs, registry scores, scan labels, gold judgments, and DOE conclusions were not used.",
      "features": [
        {
          "feature": "conditions_or_retries",
          "reason": "The request builder clamps max-results below one or above ten to bounded values before invoking the API.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "path": "scripts/tavily_search.py",
              "start_line": 34,
              "end_line": 39,
              "quote": "def clamp_max_results(value: int) -> int:\n    if value < 1:\n        return 1\n    if value > 10:\n        return 10\n    return value"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "feature": "versions_or_transformations",
          "reason": "Returned search content is converted into enumerated title/URL/score records with newline-normalized snippets limited to 280 characters.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "path": "scripts/tavily_search.py",
              "start_line": 130,
              "end_line": 147,
              "quote": "        print(\"=== RESULTS ===\")\n        for index, item in enumerate(results, start=1):\n            title = item.get(\"title\") or \"No title\"\n            url = item.get(\"url\") or \"N/A\"\n            score = item.get(\"score\")\n            content = item.get(\"content\") or \"\"\n\n            print(f\"\\n{index}. {title}\")\n            print(f\"   URL: {url}\")\n\n            if isinstance(score, (int, float)):\n                print(f\"   Score: {score:.3f}\")\n\n            if content:\n                snippet = content[:280].replace(\"\\n\", \" \").strip()\n                if len(content) > 280:\n                    snippet += \"...\"\n                print(f\"   {snippet}\")"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_closure": {
        "status": "complete_for_static_audit",
        "reason": "The invoked scripts/tavily_search.py is retained. The API, optional credential file, environment values, and queries are external/runtime interfaces. README.md includes the usage and configuration procedures; the absent LICENSE is non-operational support.",
        "local_reference_decisions": [
          {
            "target": "LICENSE",
            "classification": "illustrative_or_optional",
            "reason": "The absent LICENSE is legal support, not operational source.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "path": "README.md",
                "start_line": 185,
                "end_line": 185,
                "quote": "This project is licensed under the MIT License. See the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
