          "feature": "conditions_or_retries",
          "reason": "A full active memory triggers archival, and session startup loads existing preferences only when the file exists, otherwise assuming none.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "path": "SKILL.md",
              "start_line": 80,
              "end_line": 88,
              "quote": "### 5. Memory Limits\n- memory.md ≤100 lines\n- When full → archive old patterns to history.md\n- Merge similar entries: \"no Prettier\" + \"no ESLint\" → \"minimal tooling\"\n\n### 6. On Session Start\n1. Load `~/coding/memory.md` if exists\n2. Apply stored preferences to responses\n3. If no file exists, start with no assumptions"
            }
          ]
